  "lineage": "Twentieth-century Viennese composer-circle around Arnold Schoenberg and his students Anton Webern and Alban Berg, developing free-atonal compositional practice (c.1908-1923) followed by the twelve-tone-method serial-organization (1923 onward). Pierrot Lunaire (1912), Wozzeck (1925), and Webern's aphoristic late-period works constitute the canonical core. Distinguished from prior tonal-harmonic practice by complete suspension of triadic-tonal-hierarchy and systematic serial-row organization of pitch content.",
